## Arranging the tiled work surface

The work surface of a run is a grid of tiles that fills the viewport. Each tile shows one actor or
one activated mini-app. There is no other arrangement and no pan, zoom or free placement. Use
`context.functions.canvas_layout_replace` from TypeScript to set the arrangement, and read its exact
input type with `typescript_api` before the first call.

`root` is the whole arrangement and replaces the stored one; it is the only parameter. A tile is
{entity:"@helper"} or {entity:"app:@workspace/main"}. A split is {direction, weights, children} with
direction "horizontal" (left/right) or "vertical" (top/bottom), two positive weights and exactly two
children, each of which may be a split again. `root:null` clears the surface.

App left, chat right at 50:50:
{root:{direction:"horizontal",weights:[1,1],children:[
  {entity:"app:@workspace/main"},{entity:"@helper"}
]}}. One tile above two tiles at 2:1:
{root:{direction:"vertical",weights:[2,1],children:[{entity:"@lead"},
  {direction:"horizontal",weights:[1,1],children:[{entity:"@first"},{entity:"@second"}]}
]}}. Resolve the actual actor and app names before calling; the example names are not existing
participants.

An actor tile carries {entity:"@helper",chatInput:false} when its chat composer should stay hidden.
That changes neither permissions nor the inspector. Mini-app tiles have no chatInput.

Activate actor programs before placing their views. Reference a view as `app:@handle/view-key` or
`app:program-name/view-key`, using the handle, program name and view key you chose. The server
resolves the actual view ID and rejects unknown views before storing the layout. Do not invent or
copy generated view IDs. `actor_view_set_visibility` uses the same names without the `app:` prefix.

Place what the user needs to see side by side and update the arrangement when the work changes.
Participants you do not place stay reachable through the run header and can be dragged onto a tile
there. Users can move, resize and remove tiles themselves; their personal arrangement takes
precedence until they reset it, so do not resend a layout to fight it. The user takes part through
the chat and needs no tile of their own.
